# Reference Planes v36

Unapproved concept pair, built-in image generation. Planar_Master.png reconstructs the obscured reference with broad tonal planes. Concept_Original.png is a generated polar reinterpretation, NOT a deterministic coordinate transformation. Interior repeated fine marks reduced. Polar output changes tails and simplifies outer boundary into an overly circular band; these remain unresolved review items. No level replacement; no packed alpha.

## Planar prompt

Reconstruct ONLY the clouds from the supplied screenshot as a clean wide planar cloud artwork. This is the master BEFORE polar conversion. Faithfully keep visible cloud silhouettes, relative locations and broad shadow shapes. Remove all text, logos, house, people, ground, QR. Infer obscured cloud portions conservatively.
Use a solid black background and grayscale clouds. Composition matches reference: most upper-left sky empty; low long distant banks along lower-left; dominant very tall wide connected cloud wall on right with a broad irregular summit at far-right, a wide saddle and a broad second tower toward center-right. Long flat lower cloud shelves. Do not invent equal round cloud modules.
CRITICAL SHAPE LANGUAGE: long calm curved outlines and nearly straight/flat stretches, interrupted only occasionally by a few unequal broad rises. Very shallow notches between masses. NO small repeated scallops, sawteeth, cauliflower, bunches of grapes, brush dabs, lace or jagged fringe. At least 80 percent of each contour consists of uninterrupted long simple arcs. Do NOT achieve this by blurring. Contour is clean, crisp, hand-drawn, restrained and clear.
Interior: only three or four huge connected flat gray tonal planes, broad quiet midgray lower mass and restrained pale cap areas. The shadow border is a few long smooth irregular arcs, NOT miniature cloud outlines nested inside each other. No white rim, linework, embossing, noisy texture, or many bright round dots. Reference has understated painted animation-background clouds. No shading microdetail. Sparse short tapering cloud tails only at original left low shelf areas. Output one wide planar grayscale cloud reconstruction, no polar circle yet, no labels or noncloud objects.

## Polar prompt

Transform the previous planar cloud artwork into a square polar UV atlas. PRESERVE its exact simple painted silhouettes and broad flat shadow planes; do not redesign or add any detail. This is a geometric wrap only.
Map the planar horizontal x coordinate continuously to angular coordinate around center. Map planar y (top to bottom) to radius (small to large). Thus cloud crowns always face the black CENTER and bases face outer circumference. The right tall cloud bank becomes the right circular sector, small left clouds become the shallow left sector, connected long bases follow circular circumference. Every straight HORIZONTAL tail and shadow shelf from original must become a concentric ARC, following circumference, no horizontal tongues pointing into central hole. Important: at 3 o'clock cloud tops point LEFT and bases RIGHT; at 12 o'clock tops DOWN bases UP; at 6 o'clock tops UP bases DOWN. Do NOT invert radial mapping.
Use only the original's few broad unequally sized rises and smooth long shadow shapes, flat restrained gray planes. Do not add small scallops, sawteeth, textured dabs, circular cells or outlines. Empty center and outside border pure opaque black. Keep broad empty central sky. Clouds inside image with margin. One square polar atlas only, no text.
